# Core Beliefs

This is the philosophy of `<project>`:

1. <Imperative + one supporting clause>.

2. <...>

3. <...>

4. <...>

5. <...>

6. <...>

7. <...>

8. <...>

9. <...>

10. <...>

`<project>` will not become <category-1>, <category-2>, <category-3>, or
<category-4>. Each would invert one of the rules above.

These rules are deliberately few. When a change cannot be squared with
one of them, do not amend the rule — name the conflict, and decide which
gives.

*Companion docs: [`invariants.md`](invariants.md) for verifiable hard
constraints, [`anti-patterns.md`](anti-patterns.md) for explicit refusals.*

